mpleted chunk\nEight Lean4.21 core-only modules compose completed local bank words and bind the selected five-stage source's routing and chronological schedule.\n\nConditional-interface coverage: sequential_complete_bank composes whole local words with an endpoint universally quantified over arbitrary bank and remaining states, a common exact chart, and disjoint projectors summing to identity. It explicitly reconciles head-first physical execution with tail-first endpoint composition. Actual physical endpoints remain supplier premises.\nFinite/source-binding coverage: the literal address-factor identity route(d*tau)N = route d(N*tau^-1), exact source stage/operand metadata and replica-major schedule, retaining all60 replicas. No complete Python instance enumeration or actual census is claimed checked.\nFull-theorem coverage: no end-to-end multiplication, runtime or kappa theorem. Actual helper census, GL120/reduction/normalizer data, full-state forward/complemented-reverse words, across-replica partition, boundaries/restored selectors and costs remain open.\n\n## Explicit author-checked kappa and pins\nBase12a4934d15006e8c10f9b2264f13f8f341be802b; head005dd3f4e3cba8d1761abc4ab391aaf6d14d6f73.\nAuthor-checked selected conditional kappa = 90446448750933/125000000000000000 = 0.000723571590007464.\nThis is source-matched construction context, not a bound derived by this package. Compiler, common-ancestor chart, restored-row, routing, prime-supply, precision/recovery, complex-correctness and analytic-transfer conditions remain.\nLiteral bindings refer to research/five-stage-gen4-banks/bank_template.py, code/global_lowering.py and BANK-PROOF.md at the exact base.\n\n## Reuse and comparison\nFive supporting modules are reused unchanged: BankRouting, SplitProjectors, CoordinatePartitions, ExactFrameTransport and BankEndpoints. Three additions are SequentialCompleteBank and the two current five-stage address/schedule bindings. The composition invokes existing weighted-partition results; no novelty claim is made for generic group/partition algebra or routine list glue.\nCompared with #236's older d1d6 paired-cube finite identities/arithmetic and #487's1320-port interface: this chunk supplies the current source-specific sequential completed-bank connection, without transferring their finite instances. The complete3606-module archive of #236 was not rechecked for an exhaustive theorem comparison.\nThe construction retains PR197/PR200 completed-bank attribution, Henry Grant/hcg890 PR234 lowering, eumemic's retained source527 work, Apache-2.0 and existing assistance disclosures.\n\n## Reproduction and evidence\nFrom research/lean-sequential-bank-bindings, run python3 check.py --lean /path/to/lean-4.21.0-linux/bin/lean --build-dir /tmp/sequential-bank-check.\nLinux/Python3, fresh nonexistent output directory, offline, no Mathlib/download. Eight source hashes/imports are checked, hard per-module60s/4GiB and review45s/3.5GiB. No objects shipped.\nFresh isolated replay:12.1047compiler seconds,0.00368queue,peak VM2,266,423,296 bytes. All eight object hashes and77 complete axiom outputs match accepted evidence after explicit whitespace normalization. Independent review and both authors confirmed final scope/replay metadata.\nLocal kernel results are separate from exact-head fork CI, upstream CI and maintainer gates; those are not claimed passed. One20-file additive commit; no inherited root changes.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-11T23:10:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T23:10:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1c7bfa10b4a488d1fb94af3e353159feec3d9865","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"jamesyc:lean/sequential-bank-bindings-20261011","ref":"lean/sequential-bank-bindings-20261011","repo":{"id":1410174624,"node_id":"R_kgDOVA2OoA","name":"integer-mult-bounds","full_name":"jamesyc/integer-mult-bounds","owner":{"login":"jamesy